Bxd3 9. Qxd3 Qc7 10. Bd2 e6 11. O-O-O Ngf6 12. Kb1 O-O-O 13. c4 Bd6 14. Ne4
Nxe4 15. Qxe4 Nf6 16. Qe2 c5 17. Bc3 Rhe8 18. Rhe1 Qb6 19. Ne5 Bxe5 20. dxc5
Qc6 21. Bxe5 Qxg2 22. Bd6 Qg6+ 23. Ka1 Qf5 24. Rd3 Nd7 25. Rf3 Qh5 26. Qe3 f6
27. c6 Nb6 28. cxb7+ Kxb7 29. Qe4+ Nd5 30. Rb3+ Ka8 31. Bc7 Rc8 32. Qh1 Rxc7
33. cxd5 Rc5 34. dxe6+ Qd5 35. Qxd5+ Rxd5 36. Kb1 Re5 37. Rxe5 fxe5 38. Rg3
Rxe6 39. Rxg7 Rf6 40. Re7 Rxf2 41. Rxe5 Rf1+ 42. Kc2 Rf2+ 43. Kc3 Rf3+ {
adjudicated by Max Euwe - n.b. the result of this game was not reported in BCM
or CHESS - previously it had been believed that Aitken had been given a win
but his scorebook shows that it was a draw. This is confirmed by the entry in
the 1956/57 BCF Yearbook, p91. Note also an extra pair of moves at the end (JS,
9 May 2021)} 1/2-1/2

