1. e4 e5 2. Nf3 Nc6 3. d4 exd4 4. c3 d5 5. exd5 Qxd5 6. cxd4 Bb4+ (6... Nf6 7.
Nc3 Bb4 {was the move order according to BCM}) 7. Nc3 Nf6 (7... Bg4 8. Be2 Bxf3
(8... Nf6 9. O-O Qa5 10. Ng5 $1 Bxe2 11. Qxe2+ Be7 12. Rd1 O-O 13. d5 {()}) 9.
Bxf3 Qc4 10. Bxc6+ $1 (10. Be3 $2 Bxc3+ 11. bxc3 Qxc3+ 12. Kf1 Qc4+ 13. Kg1
Nge7 14. Rc1 Qxa2 15. Ra1 {1/2-1/2, Marshall-Capablanca, Lake Hopatcong 1926})
10... bxc6 (10... Qxc6 11. O-O Ne7 12. Qb3 Bxc3 13. bxc3 O-O 14. c4 b6 15. d5
Qg6 16. Bf4 Rac8 17. Qa4 a5 18. Qd7 $14) 11. Qe2+ Qxe2+ 12. Kxe2 O-O-O 13. Be3
Ne7 14. Rhd1 Rhe8 15. Kf3 Nf5 16. g4 $14) (7... Nge7 8. Be2 O-O 9. a3 $14 {
Penrose-Bolbochan, Moscow ol 1956}) 8. Be2 O-O (8... Ne4 9. Bd2 Bxc3 10. bxc3
Nxd2 11. Qxd2 O-O 12. Rb1 b6 13. O-O Qd6 14. Bd3 Bg4 15. Ng5 h6 16. Ne4 Qd8 17.
f4 Bf5 {(Velimirovic-Tringov, The Hague 1966)} 18. g4 $1 Bd7 (18... Bxg4 19. f5
) 19. f5 $16) 9. O-O Qa5 $2 (9... Bxc3 $2 10. bxc3 Re8 11. Re1 {^^}) (9... Qd8
$1 10. a3 Bd6 11. Bg5 h6 12. Bh4 Re8 13. d5 {Bazan-Incutto, Mar del Plata 1960}
) 10. Bd2 Rd8 (10... Nd5 11. Nxd5 Qxd5 12. Bxb4 Nxb4 13. Ne5 Be6 14. a3 Nc6 15.
Bf3 $1 $16 {Reti-Breyer, Baden 1914}) 11. a3 Be7 12. d5 $1 Nb8 (12... Nxd5 $2
13. Na4 $18) 13. Bc4 c6 14. Ne5 Qc7 15. Nxf7 $1 {["... Penrose rushed things a
bit, and it is doubtful if his speculative sacrifice should have won" (PB
Anderson, BCM]} cxd5 16. Ba2 Kxf7 17. Nxd5 $1 Nxd5 18. Qh5+ Kg8 19. Rfe1 Nc6
20. Bxd5+ Rxd5 (20... Kh8 21. Be4 h6 22. Bxh6 $1 $18) 21. Qxd5+ Kh8 22. Qf7 Bg4
23. Bc3 (23. Bb4 $145 $5) 23... Rg8 24. h3 Bc8 25. Rad1 h6 26. Rd5 Bd6 27. Qg6
{"and wins" (BCM - no more moves given)} ({Fritz suggests} 27. Rxd6 $1 Qxd6 (
27... Qxf7 28. Rxh6#) 28. Re8 $1 {with a simple mate}) 27... Be5 28. Bxe5 Nxe5
29. Rdxe5 Bd7 30. Re7 Qd8 31. Qf7 Bc6 32. R1e6 Qd1+ 33. Kh2 Qd2 34. Rg6 a6 35.
Rxg7 Qd6+ {Sources: BCM, January 1956, p2; Chessman Quarterly, Vol.3 No.17,
March/April 1971, p7} 1-0

